        "value": "critically endangered",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "The remaining speakers are elderly people spread across small villages. Adults in their 40s and 50s show only passive knowledge: they are able to understand what is being said in the language, but are not able to produce \r\neven simple messages. [The] remaining speakers use the language to speak amongst themselves, but only in very restricted situations, such as traditional events and intimate meetings. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
